From: MacFinals
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: window/focus state + main-thread rendezvous diagnostics (C06)

The 2026-11-21 capture (crashes/C06) wedged the GameThread in NtUserPeekMessage behind a
Background Worker stuck in NtUserDestroyWindow - win32u's user lock held across the mac
driver's synchronous Cocoa-main-thread rendezvous - with no way to see the focus state or the
rendezvous. This adds, following the macdrv channel and its macdrv_err_on pattern:

- macdrv_ui_on = TRACE_ON(macdrv): the new logging is OFF BY DEFAULT and enabled with
  WINEDEBUG=+macdrv (via a LogTrace twin of LogError). Always-on ERR lines fire only at
  pathological waits (OnMainThread/query > 10 s).
- Window/focus state (slot 0): applicationDidBecomeActive/ResignActive and
  windowDidBecomeKey/ResignKey track app active/inactive and the key window, each with ages;
  every transition updates the diag note and traces when enabled.
- OnMainThread (slot 1) and query: (slot 2) record the waiting tid and wait kind, cleared on
  return; the wait duration traces when enabled and ERRs above 10 s.
- OnMainThreadAsync blocks (slot 3) report which tid the main thread is executing a block
  for, so a wedged rendezvous shows both sides.

At the next wedge the stuck dump prints all of it: the focus state at the time, who was
waiting for the main thread, and what the main thread was executing.
---
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.h
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.h
@@ -23,6 +23,9 @@
 #include "macdrv_cocoa.h"
 
 #define ERR(...) do { if (macdrv_err_on) LogError(__func__, __VA_ARGS__); } while (false)
+/* C06: off-by-default focus/rendezvous tracing (WINEDEBUG=+macdrv); ERR stays always-on */
+#define UI_LOG(...) do { if (macdrv_ui_on) LogTrace(__func__, __VA_ARGS__); } while (false)
+void LogTrace(const char* func, NSString* format, ...);
 
 
